From 83ff564a9ceb639590163d864db5e874e539a939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:24:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: Report a failed runtime resume for deferred
 data

When data is sent while the device is runtime suspended,
submit_or_queue_tx_urb() anchors the URB on data->deferred and
btusb_waker() resumes the device with usb_autopm_get_interface(). If
that fails, the waker returns without a message.

An HCI command deferred during the resume can time out while the waker
is still waiting, since the command timer is already running. Report
the runtime-resume error when the PM request returns, so that the
command timeout can be correlated with the failed resume.

Leave out -EACCES, which is returned while runtime PM is disabled, for
example during a system sleep transition. Rate-limit the message, as
the waker runs once for each deferred send.
---
Tested with an emulated device attached over usbip in a QEMU guest
whose runtime resume never completes: the kernel logs, in this order,
"command 0x0c24 tx timeout" (10.09 s) and then the waker's
"Failed to resume device for deferred data: -16" (15.24 s, twice), just
before the disconnect. The unpatched kernel logs no such line.

 drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c |7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
index 95398e2ca098e..ed503eab9d566 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb_main.c
@@ -2659,8 +2659,13 @@ static void btusb_waker(struct work_struct *work)
 	int err;
 
 	err = usb_autopm_get_interface(data->intf);
-	if (err < 0)
+	if (err < 0) {
+		/* -EACCES: runtime PM is disabled, e.g. during system sleep */
+		if (err != -EACCES)
+			bt_dev_err_ratelimited(data->hdev, "Failed to resume device for deferred data: %d",
+					       err);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	usb_autopm_put_interface(data->intf);
 }

